    "Cardiovascular load scored 0–21. Each second of the day your heart rate is recorded, it's assigned to a zone (1–5). Higher zones carry more weight. The total is compressed logarithmically so 21 represents a theoretical maximum — a full day at peak intensity.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cardiovascular load scored 0–21. Each second of the day your heart rate is recorded, it's assigned to a zone (1–5). Higher zones carry more weight. The total is compressed logarithmically so 21 represents a theoretical maximum — a full day at peak intensity."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La carga sobre tu corazón a lo largo del día, en una escala de 0 a 21. Cada segundo que se registra tu frecuencia cardíaca cae en una zona (1 a 5); las zonas más altas pesan más. El total se comprime de forma logarítmica, así que 21 es un máximo teórico: un día entero a intensidad máxima."
          }
        }
      }
    },
