    "The acute:chronic workload ratio (your last week vs your last month) and training monotony describe how your load is trending. They are context for your recovery — they do NOT predict injuries; that evidence doesn't hold up. (Impellizzeri 2020)": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The acute:chronic workload ratio (your last week vs your last month) and training monotony describe how your load is trending. They are context for your recovery — they do NOT predict injuries; that evidence doesn't hold up. (Impellizzeri 2020)"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "El cociente de carga aguda:crónica (tu última semana vs tu último mes) y la monotonía describen cómo viene tu carga. Son contexto para tu recuperación — NO predicen lesiones; esa evidencia no se sostiene. (Impellizzeri 2020)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The average for your age is around %lld.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
